##Adding local files to github repo

These are the commands you use to add and push files from your local repo to your remote repository.

1 - First you add the file
```
git add filename
```

2 - Then once you have added all your new and or modified files, you create a commit

```
git commit -m "This is a message describing the commit"
```

You must always write a message with the commit. It is mandatory. The idea is that this helps you figure out what changed. 

3) Now it is time to send the commited changes to github (the remote repository)

```
git push
```
